diff --git a/CONTEXT.md b/CONTEXT.md
index c99a041..836359a 100644
--- a/CONTEXT.md
+++ b/CONTEXT.md
@@ -204,3 +204,4 @@ Guidelines below are continuously updated from internal code reviews, CodeRabbit
 131. **Modal Overlays & Focus Traps Must Not Block Root Canvas Views**: Never place full-screen blocking modals or scrim overlays (with `pointerInput { detectTapGestures { } }`) over root dashboards or navigation views when inline alternative components (e.g. `AutoSetupHeroCard`) exist. Avoid placing `.focusable()` wrappers with `focusRequester.requestFocus()` on root containers which disrupt child click hit-testing in Compose WASM, ensure web canvas keydown shortcuts handle browser defaults, and verify all SSE endpoints target `/api/v1/events/stream`.
 132. **Kotlin Multiplatform WASM Exception Handling and Global Browser Keydown Shortcuts**: In Kotlin Multiplatform / WASM, `ApiClient.safeCall` and network dispatchers MUST catch `Throwable` (`catch (e: Throwable)`) rather than `catch (e: Exception)` to ensure JS errors (`JsException`), serialization issues, and runtime WASM traps are safely caught and wrapped as `ApiResult.NetworkError` instead of crashing coroutines unhandled. When catching `Throwable`, `kotlinx.coroutines.CancellationException` MUST be explicitly caught and rethrown (`catch (e: CancellationException) { throw e }`) before `catch (e: Throwable)` to prevent breaking structured concurrency and coroutine lifecycle management. In ViewModels, async aggregation (`fetchMetrics`) MUST employ defensive error boundaries (`try/catch Throwable`) ensuring `isLoading` always transitions to `false`. Global window shortcuts (such as `Cmd+K`/`Ctrl+K` for command palette) MUST register a native `window.addEventListener('keydown', ...)` on WASM with `preventDefault()` to guarantee key events fire globally regardless of which Compose composable holds active canvas focus.
 133. **Mandatory Browser E2E Quality Gate for WASM SPA**: All frontend changes and single-binary packaging MUST be validated through the Playwright browser E2E test suite in `tests/e2e-browser/`. The CI pipeline MUST execute this suite against a running instance of the single binary (Go + embedded WASM) and verify that `#loading-screen` disappears, no unhandled JS/WASM errors are emitted in `pageerror`/`console.error`, the dashboard transitions out of loading skeletons within 5s, and global shortcuts (`Cmd+K`/`Ctrl+K`) open the command palette. Per ADR-009.
+134. **Compose WASM Dynamic Viewport Management & Null-Tolerant Collections**: In Compose Multiplatform WASM, applications MUST use `ComposeViewport(document.body!)` rather than deprecated `CanvasBasedWindow` to ensure Skiko canvas automatically resizes with dynamic browser viewports and DevTools dock/undock events without leaving blank bands. Container layouts and long views (`DashboardScreen`, `NavRail`, form screens) MUST include `Modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState())` to support vertical scrolling on constrained viewport heights. API DTOs representing collections MUST declare list fields as nullable (`items: List<T>? = emptyList()`) with safe accessors (`val items: List<T> get() = items ?: emptyList()`) to gracefully handle empty backend responses where Go marshals nil slices as `null` without throwing `kotlinx.serialization.SerializationException`.
